{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793608874,"nonce":"JaWH7lKFHeFTTpbSfMK6rx47TvU=","message":"Owner testing: (a) swipes drew nothing until the pointer left and re-entered: the window only redrew after input on request_redraw/rebuilds, not on pending prop updates; fixed in windowed.rs. (b) the second calendar swiped from the first calendar's gesture: winit on macOS reports momentum begin as TouchPhase::Started, so momentum looked like a new touch to whatever was under the pointer. New renderer/scroll_gesture.rs: gesture numbers, a touch within 80ms of a lift is momentum, momentum expires 3s after a lift, and a gesture taken by a handler-only target is latched to it. EventContext gets scroll_gesture/scroll_momentum. Calendar: swipe identity by gesture number, pointer leaving cancels (hover leave for swipes, bounds check for drags). Tests: a_swipe_belongs_to_its_calendar, leaving_cancels_a_swipe, a_drag_leaving_the_days_is_cancelled, back_to_back_swipes_each_turn_a_month; layout unit test for the momentum rule. Uncommitted.","files":null}]}